{
  "engine": "kokoro-82m-v1.0",
  "clips": [
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Ask the people in the front row if this was a happy life. They’ll tell you yes. Then they’ll ask how much time you have.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8726e21080d1dab76e443f5459e19c398c387833fa5e2a16e4db1191fb306725.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7727,
      "sha256": "cd0fe5a14d7bdb98c22bb6146f8c9ae14c53fefcb97937858b4804a1a58153b9"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Listen to this room. Somebody just laughed at a memory and then apologized. Please, keep the laugh.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/1ba63ecc05038268b6700e0a94ac8b9b660c9283684c83529fee6a2b052f9893.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7023,
      "sha256": "b0cac7b00182aeb0ecdfc133dacc4a0b854d0377c2be7b9364de30158a34e552"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Some people spend a lifetime saying, “When things settle down.” Look at this room. Things finally settled down.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/64a9742ba1e256a9ac5472cfcd6924ad9bb66158cdb64f8a31674acab1f266fa.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7919,
      "sha256": "9baa8d09e2799fbc44f5b754994451078f1bfbb655e2547ab350f92254d12e88"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "There was a wedding. There was a promise. And the person we came to bury broke it with somebody else.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/2d769a9775f67a06872c70b652441ef9efab985ff11fe41e8a276f9b9624ddfa.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6234,
      "sha256": "c829a57c630160f39a5562804cd3570251797cec2c1afc7acdfb93beabacb61d"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "There were two people in that marriage. Then there were three. The one who broke the vow is still alive.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/a2a2599f457e6cab582a7160e116bd2c5b09f1b9c7b96f59d02d12ef407f200c.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6554,
      "sha256": "c1451e332a299925467f4b2620f6bfa3131e6a56a1b3715b4ab7d66eef20b26b"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "The marriage ended before this life did. Funny how a signature can settle the house and leave the heart exactly where it was.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/e8219bac53ae98c9d90baeabe1f8e698e631b8e88756df8b081a10628234f8bf.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8623,
      "sha256": "4e3ad755e7acb753e89fe3558accab7a709ef2f0a0a012d1ba1a951104538d92"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "There’s a word in the wedding vows that nobody hears properly until a day like today. It’s the word “until.”",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/b3762c56c248488cf81ad2f279bd73cc2faee6e64365c0d14ec43ae954e4c244.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8026,
      "sha256": "ee6bcd2c60ae7900b701eadfa5375902b099702d8ea702b682f8269ab477f357"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Their daughter stayed close. Everybody keeps asking what this life amounted to. Ask her. See how long it takes her to answer.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/0cbf25dcb4a799f556f06679b7142e352e3f089e747e1b1d9c76e410c9b9f07c.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8452,
      "sha256": "03d18547929d294f9287b01fa1510b77b3c7746591213c20b01c5f546a5d192c"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Through all of it, one son stayed close. When someone asks what this life amounted to, I’d start with him.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/376e059926316c62b86dc43765d0184cf8b5d6e38c451ce975e7ed76b8d66eef.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7407,
      "sha256": "b02954cf2b9ccfdf3ec919ef03286544acf32153eb43a726f94f001c682ce881"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "There was a daughter, too. The distance between them is part of her story to tell, if she ever chooses to.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/cf4cd3c3ec10a5c4c8239fdeca985eecf395cd57f8f681de329397e71b47f654.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7002,
      "sha256": "53074aaae5e2a8fcd8ef3e9ae5186e840c57b634039070b2e000078b3227221c"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "There was a son, too. They grew apart. Imagine all the things that never quite made it into a phone call.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/6c4760f3ba5eace40dac1a86b0ce73b560cb514fcc5d397766d5fb6d19e5279f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7023,
      "sha256": "a86ecbd7b0bbda9da4a3d13fb2af723e245d395fe04b12614af04700d91f8942"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "People tell me to keep these things short. I’ll be brief. I won’t tidy up somebody’s whole life just to make it fit on this card.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/7cfaa16fc0a28f2e830875b51ebbcb60851a202ad79e8cdb4bfd1d1844c3161b.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8836,
      "sha256": "a8f38cd33f03e42917d2a302f8c86f6522ef278b97a10a00b6b2bf42ad3563d4"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "You can read every date on this program and still miss the whole person. Someone who was there can tell it better.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/09861cafd4463bc4889673527ca27b38cb69a23296687bedb568cb6d05bb4222.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7620,
      "sha256": "8e1bc93bd7cf8160cb942d6ae4fb479353e807825c757d5f2d3e55b9ad9bb09e"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I’m going to leave a little room here. Love can make a person stand up. It can also make it impossible to speak.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/1fb9e27e03f562672a3acf89dbf164fddd754a8009cbc1bd26f97867ed5b159c.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7535,
      "sha256": "1992dfc15905e9cb2732fed10ce66326f794db60f0e21db4e901580a37c39477"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Take a moment. Think of the person you nearly called on the way here. When you get outside, make the call.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/a223b0b65726d5899c5743bceb1f9a9a39e0868dc6ba43b0996f9f87dca00342.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6810,
      "sha256": "d7d03edebb765875e1685e7ba52817560b9c1167d755a3d0e0a84f967d980218"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up once. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8934f730af3ec6a567cdf29f7bb342491b7cc910548066a22bcff94c7af7d9e5.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8303,
      "sha256": "54af4a88ddaafef2222214eb0e2dbcb5b5f6c693eda7626e60fc3b76f2441a7a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up twice. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/e5686524684c27853c6b178971746dacea713d657fed6c751337f663d4669d1e.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8410,
      "sha256": "9c15ca15a85f4a5482cfab19652bad5e069958ee58c87cae00d3e4571bce63e1"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up three times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8fd874f866f0a239448c19e38e6f3d08f712a21b0a62452f655f62b4cd49fa6f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8794,
      "sha256": "57a7b4b5072fc3a757b79f949b9c0f0070a5cf64c21b953da70725d61717328c"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up four times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/ce300206a3519371a9d8a6272717af6e1472b99266f459bedb1204a4ad09b550.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8858,
      "sha256": "b05abb64de486a2c587dea7e6fa156585b33d0b7c6bf15e580aff00d16c010aa"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up five times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/14099a7188c3c96a72145b5eb1c42e3b218b37263ad658c771be4c097729e721.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8943,
      "sha256": "b2c4a8b98195e3d400b20d9ef5c36192db7cf2f12114ffa56d978833449e8c9a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "I went back through these pages. The words “let the call go to voicemail” came up six times. Somebody was on the other end.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/513e67b5e0fa4c7d188b24f39d3ff048736a15e774af3fe3f365c859a25eece5.mp3",
      "durationMs": 8836,
      "sha256": "c1c47771ddc8b6d26321183c7625737415cb439cbcf3eb4e76d84dc17f1fb9c5"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "You cheated on me. I practiced saying that without crying. Look at me. I still can’t.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/9405f6954a9eb6c5dba5620d7540334b87a9841f24120578921689551baf3419.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5274,
      "sha256": "12db67520d099767c0b69c02cc739a462df949c8a3fd78794fba6e3dfb5aac19"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "It was me. I cheated. I thought I could stand up here and just say I missed you. I do. Both things are true.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/60ce51a965c29e50ff5578ced223405e6b4eb0f60ec6624fb8011a94445bb93a.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6532,
      "sha256": "9a0dc6ebaa18fdcace1b5d78eef53471d93adcb644eac6ecee3fe1713fa86d76"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "We got divorced. I thought that meant I’d already done the losing part. Then I walked in here.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/1112a1bca1d350e362fca2ce98879554e9c7e6a19bf2c37b5b285aadbcb53be4.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5551,
      "sha256": "9d56e2fdea9812eb0ce8794b84f460849fb7d0f473d73c29ec139524f6971dde"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "We said “until death.” I had the words memorized. I never practiced what to say the day after.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/7f6ed30799c2b2ac0ceb759238a04339dc8bb4b4970429511ffc4d93112dce66.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5956,
      "sha256": "3a35876020d6aa560a50ca5ecf9beba50c46f21c53674b93b1b7ef9e9be98a0a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "The neighbor Jules carried out of the fire survived. Jules died of smoke inhalation at 46.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/97a78c2030e996ae85bb3f55c9ee2dc8f71cef78949e9a59932dbbcc76d14df5.mp3",
      "durationMs": 7258,
      "sha256": "a8f18e7ff855d1a367871f0d9d76f06eba824bf6c6b824619b42ec3b5b304fa8"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_kore",
      "voice": "af_kore",
      "text": "I kept his seat until the lights went down. At the next recital, he was there before me.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/d8e15e7b65918fa73a6e73da5a1c6e8c9cddf24ad3e2f1e69f70a8faa5328e1e.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5871,
      "sha256": "5c30ba720caf42c3a45313b8afb7c7d51459db54c53e2293fb300360310fac4b"
    },
    {
      "cast": "am_fenrir",
      "voice": "am_fenrir",
      "text": "Four months without a call. I still have the voicemail that starts, “Papa, it’s me.”",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/bc0f49d4023d7e72f199224880fdbbd4ca816019997817c9103db291cb0a61ff.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5124,
      "sha256": "cbdd9040f373936e9460d0a64d22f0b49270fc7a59f602140d2e81a5bae87e4b"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "bf_emma",
      "text": "Everyone asks me about the fire. I miss the days he came over with bread.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/650494f35f49f4ae379b668278c5a1fac807103b7d5d171297e84e3834335fec.mp3",
      "durationMs": 4527,
      "sha256": "405e3681f6775adeb5802b4fdf09bce75e072fc6d3e552fc5b28e8dadfe1131c"
    },
    {
      "cast": "am_puck",
      "voice": "am_puck",
      "text": "He said, “I was wrong,” in front of the whole team. Then he let me speak.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/d6b8fffa17cc5a7c0fbd2da02d7c5226ceb70461e36bde60ffefcfe31f74f363.mp3",
      "durationMs": 4228,
      "sha256": "773cf04b77939a9cf3599d7f03b0844db5b1f59103ecc5ffdf5d561466925987"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Jules died of heart failure at 58.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/54fb6887d91ac5d34c0d743d88011084a4179e3d4efdb5f44c311aa106aaacd8.mp3",
      "durationMs": 3162,
      "sha256": "0b1ab23a8ff8275e8ea2d07246ea8d4c41da15ef81b7448ddc2b1115178d0645"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_kore",
      "voice": "af_kore",
      "text": "He missed my recital. At the hospital he pulled up a chair for me. I stayed.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/b140eba30702b89f1024fdfebd42c84fdadcffe906f033f648bd98662ad23641.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5103,
      "sha256": "291259654c9735d072de0d19b20c8031901bc303f075f97eabba5d5d2c935988"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "At 90, Louis died in an accident.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/9e0b1e49ab296182a71589212360b31b4bf814c99f3df86704851452face2a41.mp3",
      "durationMs": 2970,
      "sha256": "5b66de409b374be0ed90985f3023b2f3a955850bfe3fa5e3222b269f2912102d"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "The telephone rang while the soup went cold. I was still waiting for you at nightfall.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/fa85ce0b4d2d93c513c9fb5c17ef593b92c9d631e27a5f86b53c602b55da1f7f.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5018,
      "sha256": "9b286a57603ae3251badaa19a6a4a3301615831f577c1beac86794c913dcb744"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "bf_emma",
      "text": "At 51, Louis kept one evening free at home. I kept the envelope with my name in pencil.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/9c0be91eaa6e6ba2c86defe956e73eb9eba939b9f28f1af602c13ac9632dab2c.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6042,
      "sha256": "c6c254e43342b40d1e538784bd016ef94705fbbd608f1fc64cc1c67f61d81b6f"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "You were 90 when you took the late meeting. The little blue chair by the door was empty.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/8b529273c661bd53624a982a6718fd34680a7f2e226a05da4a1d08071afeb352.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5146,
      "sha256": "d721db33a151266e7ffe4d8c50973548e4d8d726cfa139f65b78df6918ea182a"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "We remember Louis, who died of cancer at 82.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/727dfe4bb2ab925f076a1ca72bfc139ed336004bd30c3f173f86eb4b0154f0fe.mp3",
      "durationMs": 3631,
      "sha256": "0d670a94c6b6721f0fb9ca6e16eb43589161d8fb5ccaa2b2ef268d98b035d181"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "At 66, Louis took the late meeting. The brass key was still under the flowerpot.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/0733b74db7c0b2c200cb7717059c920614c146fe9c65ec8be25205a2c83914b3.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5252,
      "sha256": "6123c66b3a58ad9e45bd24690c7f1b79c18cb5a201766f3d0f3bde74dff895ee"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "bf_emma",
      "text": "You were 41 when you asked for help. The telephone rang while the soup went cold.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/af56af7eee2326a245a052c70896168f99ed0ca5054075682390266becde3206.mp3",
      "durationMs": 4868,
      "sha256": "52260320609c3b57857f7ca58dfb2d5a8e6c5e87692aca9c9b7e1fe4e801c073"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "That little blue chair by the door was empty. But you stayed with me, Louis.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/4b90993006214237a83b85b9088975645a5d87d9038e4c30d3d60d6347ddd1ad.mp3",
      "durationMs": 4378,
      "sha256": "6068b6fa70be664ed22f3c5f5a4c3742f4d4f25ed55b75f195118a38d3677441"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "Louis died of cancer at 89.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/01d16ee597e1e948dee5e9eeef75b267d140b1a96e3d2a40ab3455bb274cf702.mp3",
      "durationMs": 2927,
      "sha256": "ef969820b2e4dd9c9698c9b93243d8e2950c24598c340f5f2fafc916511df553"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "I still have the paper ticket from the last train. That was the evening you stayed with me.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/337d98476cf7547b6e208d4633566943d736f4b592e7f14f54df2ece23497315.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5039,
      "sha256": "13581eed5ca170c6f43a42152b1529f2fcefd46d2686e0a046f6c9608c50d6eb"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "You were 66 when you kept one evening free at home. The little blue chair by the door was empty.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/3ea5ff94037a95e9e311e90dc66a288850e601501ac06ac848269baadad502b6.mp3",
      "durationMs": 6234,
      "sha256": "c0d9fbd22b0c9a199ad09766ca26695a651e15df5c5f430054724d989b4c8ec0"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bf_emma",
      "voice": "bf_emma",
      "text": "You were 36 when you took the late meeting. I kept the envelope with my name in pencil.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/052add8aa5b31d6428b2016b3f69189ebbcd0de8a7049a634481c541786f3ff3.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5487,
      "sha256": "c4021365021fa0944ed62a05b59e4d5c4c3258312bfb49e9343b33aea39a0acd"
    },
    {
      "cast": "bm_george",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "text": "At 83, Louis died of heart disease.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/5f57d02ca82a929833d5f68171cb620f1f3101610d55b07f39ac6ed45b4e8bdc.mp3",
      "durationMs": 3268,
      "sha256": "ad2eea308d99c177c433195eef1de3175dbe4a44e83d05174dc6c66dbb2c1738"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_heart",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "You were 36 when you took the late meeting. The telephone rang while the soup went cold.",
      "src": "/audio/chapel/baf3ee9d893661000931e3a9b6851a4d7562680ccb8643c2720f899b99fc0f4d.mp3",
      "durationMs": 5402,
      "sha256": "3b2a28a902d46810b30024de18c66ef45d192cd544643afbca2c8e53b8756e09"
    },
    {
      "cast": "af_bella",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "You were 33 when you took the late meeting. The little blue chair by the door was empty.",
